<title>ITALY: Italy union heads, gov't to meet on energy policy.</title>
<headline>Italy union heads, gov't to meet on energy policy.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leaders of three of Italy's major trades union confederations will meet the government on Wednesday to discuss tariff policy and investment in the country's energy sector, union sources said.</p>
<p>The meeting, which is expected to start at 1400 GMT, will include Sergio Cofferati, secretary general of the CGIL confederation, Sergio D'Antoni of CISL and Piero Larizza of UIL.</p>
<p>Industry Minister Pier Luigi Bersani and Budget Ministry undersecretary Giorgio Macciotta will also attend.</p>
</text>
